# US-1657 — the shipped udev rule for the Nostr vendor-HID interface.
#
# Chrome's WebHID opens the device's hidraw node, and on Linux a custom VID
# owns no uaccess by default: without a rule the device is absent from (or
# unopenable in) Chrome's chooser *before any extension code runs* — the
# chooser-absent failure that is pre-grant and unowned (design §A.8.3b #1).
# Trezor (51-trezor.rules) and Ledger (50-ledger.rules) ship the same shape;
# this is ours.
#
# Install (root):
#   sudo cp 70-fapico2-nostr.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger
#
# The chooser-absent discriminating check (install guide §D16):
#   lsusb sees the device but Chrome's chooser does not  =>  this rule missing.
#
# Scoped to the fapico2 VID. The PID is NOT matched: the identity workflow
# (scripts/fix_usb_identity.py, docs/identity.md) treats PID as
# user-changeable and reflash-surviving, so a rule that bound the default
# PID would silently stop granting access after an operator re-identified
# the board.
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="fa20", TAG+="uaccess", MODE="0660", GROUP="plugdev"
